$MidnightBSD$

tcsh from https://astron.com/pub/tcsh/

The vendor branch is vendor/tcsh/dist, tagged vendor/tcsh/dist/X.YY.ZZ.
It holds pristine upstream sources trimmed with MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist; the
local changes (see below) live only on master.

To import a new release:

  1) Fetch tcsh-X.YY.ZZ.tar.gz and its .asc and verify the signature.
  2) On a checkout of vendor/tcsh/dist:
	tar -X MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist -xzf tcsh-X.YY.ZZ.tar.gz
	rsync -a --delete --exclude .git tcsh-X.YY.ZZ/ ./
	git add -A && git commit && git tag vendor/tcsh/dist/X.YY.ZZ
  3) On master:
	git merge -X subtree=contrib/tcsh vendor/tcsh/dist
  4) Bump TCSH_VERSION, TCSH_DATE and TCSH_ENGLISH_DATE in
     bin/csh/Makefile; they are substituted into patchlevel.h.in and
     tcsh.man.in in place of configure.  Compare config.h.in against
     bin/csh/config.h for new HAVE_* checks, and system/bsd4.4 against
     bin/csh/config_p.h.
  5) Build bin/csh and note the update in UPDATING.

Local changes carried on master relative to the vendor branch:

  glob.c     - #ifndef __FreeBSD__ around the case-ordering hack in
               compare(), so ranges follow LC_COLLATE.
  host.defs  - the FreeBSD block is removed, because the compiler also
               defines __FreeBSD__ and gethost would otherwise report
               FreeBSD; the MidnightBSD block carries the arch list.

Everything else we used to patch (sh.c, sh.err.c, sh.h, sh.hist.c,
sh.lex.c, tc.const.c, tc.sig.c, tc.sig.h) was adopted upstream by
6.24.16.
